Lazarus AP — provenance and licensing
=====================================

This repository combines work under three different licenses. The
summary below says which is which; individual files carry their own
headers where they differ.

1. This project's own code and documentation
--------------------------------------------
    src/, tools/, tests/, docs/*.md, docs/*.html, README.md
    Copyright (c) 2026 Lazarus AP contributors
    GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (see LICENSE).

    GPL was chosen rather than a permissive licence because parts of
    this project derive from the Virtual AGC project (below), which is
    GPL v2-or-later. Specifically, src/timing.rs is a port of
    yaShuttle/yaGPC2/src/timing.c. Licensing the whole under GPL keeps
    the combined work consistent and puts this project in the same
    licence family as the work it depends on.

2. Recovered NASA / IBM Space Shuttle material
-----------------------------------------------
    roms/nasa/RUNASM/*.asm    — the HAL/S flight runtime library
    roms/nasa/lib/*.obj       — the same, assembled by ASM101S
    roms/*/*.fcm, *.obj       — linked images of the above

    Believed to be in the public domain. Every recovered source file
    carries the header line:

        Access: Public Domain, no restrictions believed to exist.

    These files are NOT covered by this project's licence. They are
    included so that the resurrection does not depend on a toolchain
    checkout that can be deleted — as one already was.

3. Virtual AGC
---------------
    The recovered artifacts above, the HAL/S-FC compiler, the ASM101S
    assembler and the yaGPC2 cross-check emulator all exist because of
    Ron Burkey's Virtual AGC project (https://www.ibiblio.org/apollo/)
    and Don Schmidt's AP-101S work.

    The bulk of Virtual AGC is GPL v2-or-later; some components are
    declared public domain by their author (ASM101S among them). Refer
    to that project's own LICENSE.txt and to individual files.

    Derived here:
      - src/timing.rs      from yaGPC2/src/timing.c, whose own tables
                           come from the Shuttle compiler's
                           PASS2.PROCS/OBJECTGE.xpl
      - tools/lnk_lite.py  object-format handling informed by
                           ASM101S/readObject101S.py (public domain)

If you believe anything here is misattributed, please open an issue —
getting provenance right is the point of this project.
